    <content>
      <Value><![CDATA[# Understanding Templates

Templates are a crucial part of any Umbraco implementation. They define how your content is rendered to the end user.

## Key Concepts

1. **Razor Syntax**: Umbraco uses Razor for templating, allowing you to access content properties dynamically
2. **Model Access**: The Model object gives you full access to your content
3. **Layout Management**: Templates can inherit from parent templates for consistent design

## Best Practices

- Keep templates focused and modular
- Use partial views for reusable components
- Always sanitize user input with @Html.Raw() when necessary

Templates make Umbraco incredibly flexible for any design requirement.]]></Value>
    </content>
    <excerpt>
      <Value><![CDATA[Templates are the bridge between content and presentation in Umbraco. Learn how to create powerful Razor-based templates that render your content beautifully.]]></Value>
    </excerpt>
